
- Add constructors that construct with a certain capacity.
- Add reserve( )?
- The reallocation strategy must be modified.
  I have implemented scalar_list, and I believe that 
  there are inconsistencies in the non-sharing policy.
  Currently push_back of scalar_vector ensures non-sharing, while
  push_back of scalar_list assumes it. It should
  be done by a separate function that checks writability up to a certain
  capacity. This is consistent because assignment also
  does not check writability. I think the strategy in scalar_list 
  is the right one.



